{"uid":"fda79073b14dac3e","name":"test_both_peer_gates_compose_in_one_run","fullName":"tests.flows.test_flow_peer_gates#test_both_peer_gates_compose_in_one_run","historyId":"8b88f75acdae16421600adff5a91517c","time":{"start":1792160868276,"stop":1792160869683,"duration":1407},"description":"`peer_plan_review: true` + `peer_verdict_gate: true`, non-vigilant,\n    with BOTH gates driven through a real round trip in the same run: the\n    first `plan_review` invocation objects (spending approach 1's one\n    revision) and the second approves; then, after `review` verifies, the\n    `verdict_gate` invocation REJECTS carrying a genuinely non-curable\n    blocking finding (the stub's `STUB_VERDICT_GATE_REJECT_COUNT` knob,\n    same shape `test_a_verdict_gate_rejection_with_a_non_curable_finding_\n    ends_the_run_even_with_an_approach_left` drives alone). v0.21.1\n    requirement A (task 001) means that rejection parks the run in\n    `awaiting_input` RIGHT THERE (v0.36 requirement B), even with\n    `max_approaches=2` leaving a second approach available -- no archive,\n    no fresh approach, no second `verdict_gate` invocation. This is the composition `tests/test_e2e_\n    composed_gates_task032.py::test_both_peer_gates_enabled_in_the_same_\n    run` used to own (task 020, C.9), updated for requirement A: both\n    gates are still observably exercised for real (plan_review's full\n    objection-then-approval round trip, verdict_gate's real rejection),\n    just never reaching a second approach now that the rejection itself\n    ends the run instead of spending one.","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>peer_plan_review: true</code> + <code>peer_verdict_gate: true</code>, non-vigilant,<br />\nwith BOTH gates driven through a real round trip in the same run: the<br />\nfirst <code>plan_review</code> invocation objects (spending approach 1's one<br />\nrevision) and the second approves; then, after <code>review</code> verifies, the<br />\n<code>verdict_gate</code> invocation REJECTS 